    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` and wrote 71 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. I could not run coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit checks, since the only shell command allowed was the test command. Those gates are unverified. By hand, the tests exercise every branch I wrote, and I expect coverage to clear 90%. Each function is short, so CRAP should stay low. The code follows `spec.md`: region and category tables, validation that raises `ValueError`, bulk discount on `standard` lines at 10 or more (multiplied with the line discount), per-line `ROUND_HALF_UP` rounding, and credit applied to gross. The tests cover the spec's worked cases, rounding edge cases (half-up versus half-even), zero-rate and absent-rate entries in `tax_by_rate`, empty input, every validation rule including `bool` quantities, and the 2-decimal output format. I did not install anything or create files outside `solution.py` and `tests/`.",
